      "message": "fix(post): refuse a left-hand cutter on posts that cannot reverse the spindle\n\nA tool gains cutter_hand (right M3, left M4), separate from the tap's\nthread_hand. The tool gate refuses a left-hand cutter by name for every\noperation on a post that starts a spindle M3 and never reverses it\n(Haas, Tormach PathPilot, Doosan DNM, Grbl 1.1, grblHAL, Makera\nCarvera, Heidenhain, Heidenhain Klartext), at creation and as the\noperation's after-state - generation, the post, the tree and the page\nall refuse. A left-hand cutter rides the generation digest; the project\nfile steps to v83 and a .camtools library with a left-hand cutter steps\nto version 7, so an older reader refuses rather than post M3.\n\nSteps 3 and 4 (the operations read the hand and post M4) are the\nfollow-up #4102.\n\nFixes #4031",
